{"story":{"what":"TypeCollector.GetObjectInfo no longer throws when two members share a key. Each Dictionary.Add into intMembers or stringMembers now runs only if the key is not already present. After reporting the mixed-key diagnostic, the member is skipped with continue. The fallback constructor search now sorts constructors of equal accessibility by fewest parameters first; before, it put the most parameters first. The change also adds a README section on SuppressSourceGeneration, analyzer tests for suppressed types and execution tests for one suppressed type.","why":"MP-2234 reports that the analyzer stopped reporting diagnostics for [MessagePackObject(SuppressSourceGeneration = true)] types. In the base code, invalid key input such as duplicate keys made Dictionary.Add throw, so the analyzer failed and reported none of that type's diagnostics. Guarding the inserts and skipping mismatched members lets the analyzer report MsgPack005 and keep validating. The tests and README describe which diagnostics still apply to suppressed types.","touches":[{"symbol":"TypeCollector.GetObjectInfo","file":"src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs","note":"Guards intMembers/stringMembers inserts against duplicate keys, skips members whose key kind is mixed, and sorts fallback constructors by ascending parameter count."},{"symbol":"SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests","file":"tests/MessagePack.SourceGenerator.Tests/SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.cs","note":"New analyzer tests for diagnostics on suppressed types and on duplicate or mixed keys."},{"symbol":"SuppressedSourceGenerationTests","file":"tests/MessagePack.SourceGenerator.ExecutionTests/SuppressedSourceGenerationTests.cs","note":"New execution tests: no generated formatter for the suppressed type, and a round-trip through the dynamic resolver."},{"symbol":"Opting out of source generation","file":"README.md","note":"New docs section listing which analyzer rules apply to suppressed types."}]},"c